WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.134 --> 00:00:02.671
I'm a big fan of time travel stories,

00:00:02.671 --> 00:00:07.154
I love the intricacies of paradoxes, the creation of different timelines, 

00:00:07.154 --> 00:00:11.500
or if that's not the case, the changes to the single one that exists

00:00:11.903 --> 00:00:13.780
the consequences, the butterfly effect

00:00:14.144 --> 00:00:19.597
but most of all, I love the internal struggle that characters witness when they go back in time

00:00:20.153 --> 00:00:25.455
and the very visceral pain of being able to witness a broken or terrible past, but

00:00:25.896 --> 00:00:29.662
because of the risk, having to hold yourself back from changing it

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:35.291
knowing and accepting that you can't change the past, and looking towards a better future

00:00:35.636 --> 00:00:39.818
that is the primary theme that makes Link Click stand out to me

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:44.377
a new Chinese 2021 anime that has truly blown me away

00:00:45.374 --> 00:00:50.744
I'd say that I very much appreciate underrated anime, or under-appreciated rather

00:00:51.089 --> 00:00:55.823
Hence my love for say, Space Brothers, or Mushishi, or the recent Odd Taxi

00:00:55.823 --> 00:01:01.173
which like Link Click, went largely under the radar amidst Spring 2021 anime

00:01:01.786 --> 00:01:06.580
but while Odd Taxi is just an anime of the season for me, or maybe even the year

00:01:06.925 --> 00:01:11.845
Link Click is even further along the spectrum and genuinely stood out to me

00:01:11.998 --> 00:01:15.627
as what could possibly become one of my all time favorite anime

00:01:16.145 --> 00:01:16.878
yeah.

00:01:17.741 --> 00:01:19.033
watch this show

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:24.510
it follows two main characters, the brains: calm and collected Lu Guang

00:01:24.778 --> 00:01:30.684
and the more headstrong and ambitious–forgive me for my pronunciation– Cheng Xiaoshi

00:01:31.106 --> 00:01:36.245
who i'll refer to as Cheng from now on for the sake of the ears of any of Chinese-speaking viewers right now

00:01:36.763 --> 00:01:40.904
if you couldn't tell by the name, it is a Donghua, or a Chinese anime

00:01:41.230 --> 00:01:46.311
a category which in the past few years, has had a number of breakthroughs in mainstream anime

00:01:46.311 --> 00:01:48.426
the most notable being the King's Avatar

00:01:49.001 --> 00:01:52.978
and I personally, I'm rather ashamed to say it, I've never watched one before

00:01:53.323 --> 00:01:55.372
so I figured now was the time to start

00:01:55.717 --> 00:02:01.431
and whether this show is an anomaly, or a true representation of the standard that Donghua reach,

00:02:01.680 --> 00:02:06.461
this category of show has totally earned my respect, it was simply that good

00:02:07.151 --> 00:02:14.089
now, Lu Guang and Cheng run a small shop called the Time Photo Studio, that fronts as a simple photo development store

00:02:14.377 --> 00:02:20.777
however, their main job is traveling into photos given by their clients for various reasons

00:02:21.026 --> 00:02:25.222
to collect information from someone's boss, say goodbye to a past lover, 

00:02:25.835 --> 00:02:30.000
they enter photos into past memories of people and look for information

00:02:30.767 --> 00:02:35.300
now, Lu Guang is able to see the 12 hour time frame after the photo was taken

00:02:36.009 --> 00:02:41.229
the timeline, every moment that happens–he essentially becomes this omniscient viewer

00:02:41.862 --> 00:02:45.753
meanwhile, Cheng enters the photo in the body of the photo-taker

00:02:46.253 --> 00:02:51.258
Lu Guang constantly informs Cheng of what he has to do to make sure he doesn't change the timeline at all

00:02:51.641 --> 00:02:54.345
from ways he has to act, to words he has to say

00:02:54.748 --> 00:03:00.000
all the while Cheng has to make sure he does the job, and collects whatever information the client needs

00:03:00.556 --> 00:03:03.869
the overall concept is rather simple at surface level

00:03:04.195 --> 00:03:08.490
enter the photo and do the task you need to, without changing anything

00:03:09.199 --> 00:03:14.441
one of the lines Lu Guang, the calm and collected one, always says goes along the lines of 

00:03:14.537 --> 00:03:18.296
"We don't change the past for the sake of changing the future"

00:03:20.405 --> 00:03:24.339
and first I must mention the awesome dynamic between Lu Guang and Cheng

00:03:24.607 --> 00:03:30.225
aside from the very obvious Ying &amp; Yang imagery of their hair, they are really just that

00:03:30.589 --> 00:03:32.872
opposites that complete each other

00:03:33.198 --> 00:03:40.000
without Cheng, they can't enter photos, but without Lu Guang, Cheng would inevitably change the timeline completely

00:03:40.805 --> 00:03:43.725
return to a life that he doesn't even know

00:03:44.070 --> 00:03:45.473
headstrong vs collected

00:03:45.914 --> 00:03:47.476
ambitious vs reserved

00:03:48.128 --> 00:03:52.214
and this dynamic, this dichotomy inevitably leads to conflict

00:03:52.827 --> 00:03:58.291
because Cheng upon entering the body of the photo-taker experiences their emotions as well

00:03:58.866 --> 00:04:02.898
how they feel at the moment, and should the photo be steeped in tragedy, 

00:04:02.994 --> 00:04:07.251
then the urge to change things, to make them better, becomes stronger,

00:04:07.251 --> 00:04:10.166
and more difficult to avoid for the headstrong Cheng

00:04:10.856 --> 00:04:14.677
but, while this is the makings for a rather annoying character at surface level,

00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:21.698
being the one who can't follow the rules and is constantly trying to change the timeline, Cheng has actually done extremely well

00:04:22.062 --> 00:04:24.442
I actually like him more than Lu Guang

00:04:24.710 --> 00:04:31.169
it's hard to go into all of it without spoiling, but the combination of him being in the literal shoes of the characters

00:04:31.572 --> 00:04:33.495
as well as the events he's put through, 

00:04:33.936 --> 00:04:39.169
you really end of sympathizing with him, because in a way he is the only one suffering here 

00:04:39.706 --> 00:04:42.486
the clients have already lived through these memories

00:04:42.908 --> 00:04:48.829
Lu Guang knows the events from start to finish, and how it should go–he's disconnected from the story

00:04:49.193 --> 00:04:56.581
but Cheng is the one who has to relive it, regardless of whether the end to that 12 hour time frame is good or bad

00:04:57.099 --> 00:05:03.771
for Lu Guang, it's just a job, but for Cheng, it's his life and someone else's that he is embodying

00:05:04.269 --> 00:05:09.502
and to go through that and accept a terrible end is very difficult and inevitably 

00:05:09.732 --> 00:05:13.797
the idea of changing the past becomes the central conflict of the show

00:05:15.522 --> 00:05:21.464
again, I have to reiterate for any time travel buffs, any Steins Gate fans, or Vivy fans, or Re:Zero fans;

00:05:21.579 --> 00:05:22.616
I think you'll love this show

00:05:23.364 --> 00:05:29.764
the time travel is done very well, it's explained clearly without having any holes that I noticed, or anything like that

00:05:30.416 --> 00:05:35.787
the show itself, aside from the central concept, is also just put together very, very well

00:05:36.515 --> 00:05:39.901
it's widescreen, which often isn't seen in anime honestly

00:05:40.284 --> 00:05:44.021
I can personally only think of the Monogatari series of the top of my head

00:05:44.749 --> 00:05:48.568
but in Link Click, along with the great animation and the widescreen,

00:05:48.568 --> 00:05:52.868
it works together to make this very cinematic and artistic feel to it visually

00:05:53.577 --> 00:05:58.285
the first episode has a food-making scene, a staple of any well animated movie

00:05:58.611 --> 00:05:59.111
like

00:05:59.341 --> 00:06:02.806
ALL of the anime movies have it for some reason, I don't even know why

00:06:03.688 --> 00:06:07.736
and the animation just stays consistently strong, it never falters

00:06:08.043 --> 00:06:12.857
I mean, they even have a whole episode where it's just Cheng playing basketball in someone else's body

00:06:12.857 --> 00:06:17.651
and it's animated like, almost better than half the games in Kuroko no Basket

00:06:18.437 --> 00:06:20.917
it is very, very visually pleasing

00:06:21.205 --> 00:06:23.948
and plus, on my mandatory OST rant

00:06:24.370 --> 00:06:28.589
the OST itself isn't necessarily top tier–it's good don't get me wrong– 

00:06:28.819 --> 00:06:34.188
but the opening and ending are awesome, it's where the show really shines sonically

00:06:35.000 --> 00:06:38.447
the opening is this funky english track where the characters are tutting,

00:06:38.447 --> 00:06:43.169
it has like a similar feel to Jujustu Kaisen's ending, with real human-like dancing

00:06:43.437 --> 00:06:45.183
and the song is great of course

00:06:45.451 --> 00:06:51.382
and the ending is this dope Chinese hip hop track, that always gets built up to at the end of each episode

00:06:52.053 --> 00:06:57.986
almost every episode ends on some kind of dramatic note or cliff hanger, and the ending just eases right in

00:06:57.986 --> 00:06:58.908
listen to this:

00:06:58.908 --> 00:07:10.286
*OverThink by Fan Ka playing*

00:07:10.286 --> 00:07:14.466
but to return to that idea of Link Click having a cinematic feel to it,

00:07:14.792 --> 00:07:20.640
even more than just aesthetically, this show is almost like multiple movies put into a single series

00:07:21.292 --> 00:07:27.129
each client, or each photo, that Lu Guang and Cheng go into feels like a single movie in itself

00:07:27.493 --> 00:07:30.738
it tells a complete story through these characters' past

00:07:31.754 --> 00:07:35.589
for example, here I will briefly discuss what happens in the side story episode,  

00:07:35.589 --> 00:07:40.000
which is technically an add-on to the 11 episode series, so I'm trying to avoid spoilers

00:07:40.000 --> 00:07:44.736
while making sure to give you a rather, holistic view on what happens in each episode

00:07:45.675 --> 00:07:51.197
now here the two boys receive an image from a man, who loves this girl from a strict martial arts family 

00:07:51.465 --> 00:07:54.572
and he can only marry her if he beats her father in battle

00:07:55.224 --> 00:07:59.409
despite him not being from a martial arts family, and the girl being older than him,

00:07:59.601 --> 00:08:04.241
year after year he walks up to the mountain to their temple, and feudally fights her father 

00:08:04.817 --> 00:08:10.311
now Cheng goes into the photo to figure out the key to beating him, what the father's hidden technique is

00:08:10.982 --> 00:08:16.831
as he fights, and Lu Guang of course tells him how to avoid the hits and survive since he knows what'll happen,

00:08:17.234 --> 00:08:20.734
he feels the perseverance and feelings of the man towards his lover

00:08:21.290 --> 00:08:23.676
what keeps pushing him year after year

00:08:24.385 --> 00:08:29.421
and unfortunately, it's revealed in the past that there is, in fact, another man who wishes to wed her

00:08:30.130 --> 00:08:33.080
so this is our client's last chance

00:08:33.941 --> 00:08:40.000
but, Cheng couldn't figure it out, he ends the 12 hour time frame without ever figuring out what it was

00:08:40.422 --> 00:08:45.435
so after they leave the photo, they return to the man, who they've never met, they got the photo without seeing him

00:08:46.048 --> 00:08:51.995
only to realize now that the young man, who you expected to be just a year older than said photo, trying again

00:08:52.417 --> 00:08:57.268
is in fact a man now well into his years, a father, a grandfather even

00:08:57.996 --> 00:09:03.096
he never once figured out how to win, but has run a dojo for years now because he never gave up

00:09:03.269 --> 00:09:06.216
and continues climbing those stairs every year

00:09:06.695 --> 00:09:08.663
it's heartbreaking and beautiful 

00:09:09.185 --> 00:09:13.292
knowing that this photo that he sent them, was just a last ditch effort

00:09:13.944 --> 00:09:20.000
that he's tried all this time without ever knowing how to win, and they take him up one last time to the top of the mountain, and...

00:09:20.748 --> 00:09:23.246
on second thought actually, I won't spoil the end

00:09:23.687 --> 00:09:24.547
just watch the show :)

00:09:26.023 --> 00:09:33.640
but you can see how emotional Link Click can get, because the entire premise is essentially using the past to make a better future

00:09:34.349 --> 00:09:40.423
and there actually is an overarching plot that is drenched in mystery and intrigue that comes by every so often

00:09:40.423 --> 00:09:43.511
so it's not just episodic, if you don't like that

00:09:44.393 --> 00:09:46.719
I really can't praise this show enough

00:09:47.141 --> 00:09:53.181
I might even make a more deep, philosophical type video about it once it's finished and has time to marinate in my mind

00:09:53.909 --> 00:09:57.388
but I just had to get this out now, cause I wanna make sure people hear about it

00:09:57.982 --> 00:10:02.852
I mean, I don't even remember how I found it yesterday afternoon, but I couldn't stop watching after I started

00:10:03.216 --> 00:10:07.877
I feel like because it's an ONA, not Japanese, it's naturally goes under the radar more

00:10:07.877 --> 00:10:08.626
but, but

00:10:08.626 --> 00:10:10.000
please, give it a try

00:10:11.169 --> 00:10:15.617
it is awesome, it's emotional, it's dramatic and intense, and I just love it

00:10:15.617 --> 00:10:21.695
I've loved it since the start, and hopefully by the time it finishes, in two episodes, I'll love it to the very end

00:10:22.768 --> 00:10:24.833
what do you guys think? have any of you watched it?

00:10:24.833 --> 00:10:27.041
if so, do you like it as much as I do?

00:10:27.367 --> 00:10:32.464
you might not, I'm a big time travel guy, and animation so it really just hit all the bases for me

00:10:33.001 --> 00:10:34.265
leave a comment down below

00:10:35.319 --> 00:10:37.325
as always, this has been the Anime Culture Corner

00:10:37.325 --> 00:10:43.005
